		rdfs:label	"Specialty Pharma"@en ;
		skos:definition	"This industry includes companies that specialize in developing, manufacturing and marketing pharmaceuticals. Typically, these companies are less R&D focused and more marketing driven. They may seek M&A activities to expand their drug portfolios or vertically integrate. Furthermore, these companies engage in less risky drug developments, such as reformulations and branded generics. Some common products include botanical-based medicine, nutraceuticals, over-the-counter (OTC) drugs and veterinary medicine."@en ;
		skos:notation	"151012" ;
		tempo:validFrom	"2014-08-08"^^xsd:date ;
